+ "reflection": {
+  "type": "何时离开",
+  "scenario": {
+   "zh": "虚构：六个人的咖啡店后场团队，年底分红由店长一人定，方案照入职年限排。一位从别家跳槽来的烘豆师改进了拼配，出品口碑最好，却分得最少；店里已有传言，说店长只照顾老员工。",
+   "en": "Fictional: a six-person back-of-house team at a coffee shop. The year-end bonus is set by the store manager alone, ranked by years of service. A roaster lured over from another shop improved the house blend and earns the best word of mouth for the drinks, yet gets the smallest share. Talk in the shop has it that the manager only looks after the old hands."
+  },
+  "question": {
+   "zh": "这位烘豆师应该留下来把分配规则谈清楚，还是另找一家店？留下意味着当那个挑刺的人，未必改得动，还可能被贴标签；离开干净利落，却等于默认这套规矩，也放弃了已经积累的手感和熟客。",
+   "en": "Should the roaster stay and get the allocation rule out into the open, or look for another shop? Staying means being the one who picks at things — it may change nothing and earn him a label. Leaving is clean and quick, but it effectively concedes the rulebook and gives up the feel for the coffee and the regulars he has built up."
+  },
+  "example": {
+   "assumptions": {
+    "zh": "假设他手里有硬数据（近两个月各人排班、出品与差评记录），店长并非恶意，只是惯性加怕麻烦；假设本地还有两三家店可以去。",
+    "en": "Assume he has hard data — two months of everyone's schedules, output and complaint records — and that the manager is not malicious, merely set in his ways and averse to trouble. Assume two or three other shops locally he could move to."
+   },
+   "steps": {
+    "zh": "先把排班与出品记录整理成一张表，只列事实；约店长单独谈一次，只谈规则口径，不谈人身；给出下次分红可采用的透明算法和一个过渡方案；若店长连列数据都不接受，再谈去留。",
+    "en": "First turn the schedules and output records into one table, facts only. Book a one-on-one with the manager and talk about the rule, never about personalities. Offer a transparent algorithm for the next bonus round plus a transitional arrangement. If the manager will not even look at the numbers, then discuss whether to stay or go."
+   },
+   "alternative": {
+    "zh": "另一种合理选择是直接走人，去一家分配有成文规则的店。理由是信任一旦塌了，重建的成本全由个人承担，而离开本身也是给店方和同行的信号。两种都合理，取决于他怎么判断这家店还有没有得改。",
+    "en": "A reasonable alternative is simply to leave for a shop where written rules govern payouts. The argument: once trust has collapsed, the cost of rebuilding it falls entirely on the individual, and leaving is itself a signal to the shop and to the trade. Both choices are sound; it turns on how he judges whether this shop can still be changed."
+   }
+  }
+ },
+ "uncertainty_note": {
+  "zh": "全部材料出自司马迁《史记·陈丞相世家》《项羽本纪》《淮阴侯列传》以及班固《汉书》据《史记》的改写（A-E10 与 A-E4 同源），没有真正独立的第二史源；韩信评项王（A-E20）与陈平析项王（A-E2）虽可对照，但同出司马迁，不是互证。「太牢具—恶草具」一幕高度戏剧化，无从核对；「范增因反间而去」是《史记》给出的因果叙述（疑心→不听其计→求去→道中病死），不是独立证据；范增求去的原话两篇措辞不同（《陈丞相世家》作「願請骸骨歸」，《项羽本纪》作「願賜骸骨歸卒伍」）；陈平陈述的离魏、离楚理由出自他对汉王的自述，可能带有自我辩护成分（作者推断）；「盗嫂」「受诸将金」只是汉营诸将的指控，无独立核实；韩信「数以策干项羽」的具体内容原文未载；项羽、范增、韩信的内心活动原文未载，本文未写。本文只说韩信离开在「汉王之入蜀」时，早于陈平投汉，不另系具体年月。「汉之三年」折算为公元前204年依通行纪年，不出自本篇证据。",
+  "en": "All materials come from Sima Qian's Shiji — the Hereditary House of Chancellor Chen, the Basic Annals of Xiang Yu, and the Memoir of the Marquis of Huaiyin — and from Ban Gu's Han Shu, which reworks the Shiji (A-E10 and A-E4 derive from the same account). There is no genuinely independent second source. Han Xin's verdict on the King of Chu (A-E20) and Chen Ping's analysis of him (A-E2) can be set side by side, but both come from Sima Qian and do not corroborate one another. The \"fine dishes — coarse fare\" scene is highly dramatic and cannot be verified. That \"Fan Zeng left because of the stratagem of mistrust\" is the causal narrative the Shiji gives (suspicion → his advice not followed → request to leave → death by illness on the road), not independent evidence. Fan Zeng's request to leave is worded differently in the two chapters (the Hereditary House of Chancellor Chen has \"I ask to resign and take my old bones home\"; the Basic Annals of Xiang Yu has \"grant me my bones to return to the ranks\"). Chen Ping's stated reasons for leaving Wei and leaving Chu are his own account to the King of Han and may carry self-justification (author's inference). \"Seducing his elder brother's wife\" and \"taking the generals' money\" are accusations made by generals in the Han camp, with no independent verification. The substance of Han Xin's \"repeatedly pressed Xiang Yu with strategies\" is not recorded. The inner thoughts of Xiang Yu, Fan Zeng and Han Xin are not recorded and are not written here. This piece says only that Han Xin left at \"the King of Han's entry into Shu,\" earlier than Chen Ping's defection, and assigns no specific date to it. \"The third year of the Han\" is converted to 204 BC by the conventional chronology; that conversion does not come from the evidence in this piece."
+ },
