+ "revision": 1,
+ "title": {
+  "zh": "拆掉水泵把手，宽街的霍乱就停了吗？",
+  "en": "Did Removing the Pump Handle Stop the Broad Street Cholera?"
+ },
+ "dek": {
+  "zh": "1854年伦敦宽街，一口公共水泵的把手被拆掉。提出建议的医生自己提醒：病例在那之前已经在下降。把证据链补上的，是一位本以为能推翻水泵说的牧师。",
+  "en": "In 1854 the handle of a public pump on Broad Street, London, was taken off. The doctor behind it pointed out that cases were already falling. The evidence was completed by a clergyman who expected to disprove the pump theory."
+ },
+ "sections": [
+  {
+   "id": "hook",
+   "heading": {
+    "zh": "十天，五百人，一口井",
+    "en": "Ten Days, Five Hundred Dead, One Well"
+   },
+   "paras": [
+    {
+     "zh": "1854年8月31日起，伦敦宽街一带突然暴发霍乱。按斯诺的统计，剑桥街与宽街交汇处250码以内，十天里有五百多人因霍乱死亡；不到六天，灾情最重的几条街走空了四分之三以上的居民。",
+     "en": "From 31 August 1854, cholera broke out around Broad Street in London. By John Snow's count, within 250 yards of the corner of Cambridge Street and Broad Street more than five hundred people died of cholera in ten days. In less than six days, the worst-hit streets were deserted by more than three-quarters of their inhabitants.",
+     "kind": "record",
+     "ev": [
+      "B-E1",
+      "B-E7",
+      "B-E14"
+     ]
+    },
+    {
+     "zh": "医生约翰·斯诺怀疑街角那口公共水泵。他拿不出能给人看的病原体，只有死亡名单和打听来的饮水情况：在这口泵供水的范围内，有61名死者据说常喝或偶尔喝宽街泵水，6例因亲友死的死、走的走而问不到，6例据说发病前不喝。",
+     "en": "Dr John Snow suspected the public pump on the corner. He had no germ to show anyone, only a list of the dead and what he could learn about what they drank. In the area the pump served, he was told that 61 of the dead had drunk Broad Street pump water, regularly or now and then; in 6 cases nobody connected with the dead could be found; and in 6 he was told they had not drunk it before falling ill.",
+     "kind": "record",
+     "ev": [
+      "B-E2"
+     ]
+    }
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "id": "context",
+   "heading": {
+    "zh": "时间、地点、人物",
+    "en": "Time, Place, People"
+   },
+   "paras": [
+    {
+     "zh": "地点是伦敦威斯敏斯特的圣詹姆斯教区。能下令处置水泵的是教区济贫委员会；教区的霍乱调查委员会后来增补了两名成员：斯诺，和亨利·怀特黑德牧师。当时还没有今天的细菌学说，斯诺只能说水里有“霍乱毒物”，它是什么、怎样致病，谁也拿不出实物。",
+     "en": "The place was the parish of St James, Westminster. The body that could act on the pump was the parish Board of Guardians; the parish's Cholera Inquiry Committee later added two members: Snow and the Reverend Henry Whitehead. Germ theory did not yet exist. Snow could only speak of a \"cholera poison\" in the water; nobody could show what it was or how it worked.",
+     "kind": "record",
+     "ev": [
+      "B-E3",
+      "B-E8",
+      "B-E16"
+     ]
+    }
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "id": "story",
+   "heading": {
+    "zh": "先问谁没事",
+    "en": "First Ask Who Was Fine"
+   },
+   "paras": [
+    {
+     "zh": "斯诺还去看谁没事。波兰街济贫院四分之三以上被死过人的房子包围，535名在院者只有5人死于霍乱；院里有自己的泵井，从不去宽街取水。按周围街道的死亡率，这里本该死一百多人。宽街啤酒厂有七十多名工人，没有人重症，只有两人轻微不适；老板说工人有麦芽酒配给，他相信他们根本不喝水，厂里还有一口深井。",
+     "en": "Snow also looked at who was spared. The workhouse in Poland Street was more than three-quarters surrounded by houses where people had died of cholera, yet of its 535 inmates only 5 died of it. It had its own pump-well and never sent to Broad Street for water; at the death rate of the surrounding streets, more than a hundred would have died there. The brewery on Broad Street had more than seventy workmen; none fell seriously ill and only two were slightly unwell. The owner said the men had an allowance of malt liquor and he believed they did not drink water at all; the brewery also had a deep well of its own.",
+     "kind": "record",
+     "ev": [
+      "B-E4",
+      "B-E5"
+     ]
+    },
+    {
+     "zh": "最能说明问题的病例不在宽街。住在汉普斯特德西区的E太太几个月没到过宽街一带，只是喜欢那口泵的水，每天有车从宽街出发，给她捎一大瓶。8月31日捎来的水，她当晚喝了，周五又喝，周五傍晚发病，周六去世。来看她的侄女也喝了这水，回到伊斯灵顿地势高、环境好的家中后发病身亡。斯诺注明，当时这两处都没有霍乱。",
+     "en": "The most telling case was not on Broad Street at all. Mrs E, who lived at West End, Hampstead, had not been near Broad Street for months, but she liked the water from that pump, and a cart going out from Broad Street each day brought her a large bottle. She drank the water brought on 31 August that evening and again on Friday, fell ill on Friday evening and died on Saturday. Her niece, who was visiting, drank it too; she went home to a high, healthy part of Islington, fell ill and also died. Snow noted that there was no cholera at the time in either place.",
+     "kind": "record",
+     "ev": [
+      "B-E9"
+     ]
+    },
+    {
+     "zh": "9月7日晚，斯诺向教区济贫委员会陈述了这些情况，第二天，水泵把手被拆下。但他自己的统计显示，疫情在那之前已经转弱：每天新发病例从143降到116，再到54；把手拆下的9月8日，新发是12例。斯诺写道，到9月8日每日死亡已大为减少，井水“很可能”因为某种原因已经不再含有霍乱毒物。",
+     "en": "On the evening of 7 September Snow laid these facts before the parish Board of Guardians, and the next day the pump handle was removed. Yet his own figures show the outbreak was already weakening: new attacks fell from 143 a day to 116, then to 54, and on 8 September, the day the handle came off, there were 12. Snow wrote that \"the daily number of fatal attacks was already much diminished by September the 8th\" and that \"it is not improbable that the water had, from some cause or other, ceased to contain the cholera poison\".",
+     "kind": "record",
+     "ev": [
+      "B-E3",
+      "B-E6",
+      "B-E8"
+     ]
+    },
+    {
+     "zh": "怀特黑德牧师起初并不相信。他后来写道，刚听说暴发被归咎于水泵时，他对一位医生朋友说，仔细调查会推翻这种说法；他也坚持把每个难解的病例查到底：“这个问题太重要，不能为了一套理论的整齐而牺牲。”转折出现在他为别的事翻阅登记署周报的时候：宽街40号一个五个月大的女婴，9月2日死亡，死前腹泻已四天。他认识这家人，却一直没问她何时发病。他立刻上门，从孩子母亲那里得知：女婴8月28日发病，排泄物到8月30日停止；洗尿布的水，一部分倒进后院水槽，一部分倒进前院的化粪池，而化粪池紧挨着泵井。他马上报告委员会，委员会下令调查，结果“清楚地确立”了化粪池液体渗入井中的事实。",
+     "en": "The Reverend Henry Whitehead started out a sceptic. He later wrote that when he first heard the outbreak blamed on the pump, he told a medical friend that a careful investigation would disprove that theory; and he insisted on chasing every awkward case: \"It is far too important a subject to be sacrificed to the symmetry of a theory.\" The turn came while he was reading the Registrar's returns for another purpose. An entry recorded the death on 2 September of a five-month-old girl at 40 Broad Street, after four days of diarrhoea. He knew the family but had never asked when she fell ill. He went straight to the house. The mother told him the baby had been taken ill on 28 August and that the discharges stopped on 30 August; the water used to soak her napkins had been poured partly into a sink in the back yard and partly into a cesspool in the front area, close to the pump well. He reported this to the committee, which ordered an inquiry. It \"clearly established the general fact of percolation of fluid from the cesspool into the well\".",
+     "kind": "record",
+     "ev": [
+      "B-E10",
+      "B-E11",
+      "B-E12",
+      "B-E13"
+     ]
+    },
+    {
+     "zh": "1855年，委员会一致认为，“霍乱区”内8月31日起那几天突然、猛烈而集中的暴发，“以某种方式”归因于饮用该井的不洁之水；至于水是怎样起作用的，委员会明确表示不支持任何一种假说。",
+     "en": "In 1855 the committee was \"unanimously of opinion\" that the sudden, severe and concentrated outbreak in the \"Cholera area\" from 31 August \"was in some manner attributable to the use of the impure water of the well\". On how the water acted, it refrained \"from expressing an opinion in favour of any hypothesis\".",
+     "kind": "record",
+     "ev": [
+      "B-E14",
+      "B-E15"
+     ]
+    }
