+ "reflection": {
+  "type": "不确定下决策（项目中途如何评估）",
+  "scenario": {
+   "zh": "一家公司的三年期数据工程外派培养计划进行到第二年半，业务线主管反映学员“文化上不像自己人”，而学员刚要进入核心项目。",
+   "en": "A company's three-year data-engineering overseas training program is two and a half years in. The business line head reports that the participants \"don't feel like one of us culturally,\" while the participants are just about to enter core projects."
+  },
+  "question": {
+   "zh": "中途评估一个长期培养计划时，如果“是否融入组织文化”和“专业产出何时兑现”指向相反结论，该以什么证据决定继续、收缩还是叫停？谁有资格下这个判断？",
+   "en": "When reviewing a long-term training program mid-way, if \"does it fit the organizational culture\" and \"when will professional output pay off\" point to opposite conclusions, on what evidence should we decide to continue, cut back, or stop? Who is qualified to make that judgment?"
+  },
+  "example": {
+   "assumptions": {
+    "zh": "计划目标是培养能独立负责核心系统的人才，三年为约定期限，已有两年半的过程数据；文化感受主要是印象，专业产出有可核对的记录。",
+    "en": "The program's goal is to develop people who can independently take charge of core systems; three years is the agreed term, and two and a half years of process data already exist. The cultural impressions are mostly impressions; the professional output has checkable records."
+   },
+   "steps": {
+    "zh": "先把两类指标分开列：可核对的产出（交付、考核、证书）与主观印象（“像不像自己人”），分开计分；让用人方、执行方、学员三方到场陈述；最后设定明确的兑现时间点和止损线，再决定是否继续。",
+    "en": "First list the two kinds of indicators separately: checkable output (deliverables, assessments, certificates) and subjective impressions (\"are they like us\"), scored separately. Have the hiring side, the implementing side and the participants all state their cases at the meeting. Finally, set a clear payoff point and a stop-loss line before deciding whether to continue."
+   },
+   "alternative": {
+    "zh": "另一种合理选择是立即收缩、只留少数人走完最后半年：理由是文化摩擦已经影响团队协作，即便专业产出即将兑现，组织代价也可能太高。这是作者提出的替代方案。",
+    "en": "Another reasonable option is to cut back right away and keep only a few people for the last six months: the reason being that the cultural friction has already affected teamwork, and even if the professional output is about to pay off, the organizational cost may be too high. This alternative is proposed by the author."
+   }
+  }
+ },
+ "uncertainty_note": {
+  "zh": "撤回奏折原文本篇未取得；撤回的经过与理由主要出自容闳（Yung Wing）1909年回忆录，他是当事一方，对陈兰彬与 Woo Tsze Tung 有强烈敌意，其转述的 Woo 报告内容、御史奏请的动机、美国排华氛围均未经独立佐证。波特等人的抗议信文本经容闳书转载，未见原件。Woo Tsze Tung 一般认为即吴子登，但本证据包未直接证明该对应，列为待核实。詹天佑履历出自1917年《游美同学录》，为单一来源；其1881年获耶鲁土木工程学士、同年回国属该书记载（光绪七年）。陈兰彬与容闳争执事项的列举出自容闳单方记述。人名对应：陈兰彬即容闳书中的 Chin Lan Pin，《清史纪事本末》误作“陳蘭斌”，并把容闳误作“容閑”；这类对应属通行考订，非本篇证据直接给出。",
+  "en": "The original text of the recall memorial was not obtained for this piece. The course of and reasons for the recall come mainly from Yung Wing's 1909 memoir; he was one of the parties involved and was strongly hostile to Chen Lanbin and Woo Tsze Tung. The contents of Woo's reports as retold by him, the censor's motives for his memorial, and the anti-Chinese atmosphere in America are all uncorroborated by independent sources. The text of the protest by Porter and others survives only as reprinted in Yung Wing's book; no original has been seen. Woo Tsze Tung is generally taken to be Wu Zideng, but this evidence packet does not directly establish the identification, so it is listed as to be verified. Zhan Tianyou's record comes from the 1917 Record of Students Returned from America, a single source; his 1881 Yale bachelor's degree in civil engineering and his return home the same year are as recorded there (seventh year of Guangxu). The list of disputes between Chen Lanbin and Yung Wing comes from Yung Wing's one-sided account. Name identifications: Chen Lanbin is Yung Wing's \"Chin Lan Pin\"; the Qing history spells him 陳蘭斌 and Yung Wing 容閑, both slips. These identifications follow standard scholarship and are not stated in the evidence itself."
+ },
